* parameter file for CG polymers
*
* Date: Oct 8, 2026
* Author: Shanlong Li

BOND
!
!V(bond) = Kb(b - b0)**2
!
!Kb: kcal/mole/A**2
!b0: A
!
!converted from GROMACS (b0 nm, kb kJ/mol/nm**2): Kb = kb/(2*4.184*100), b0 = 10*b0
!
!atom type Kb          b0
!
!bonds for methacrylate polymers (QDM, BZM)
MMA   MMA    17.93      2.79   ! A-A, 0.279 15000
MMA   MAO    23.90      2.82   ! A-B, 0.282 20000
MAO   NC4    17.93      4.00   ! B-C, 0.400 15000
MAO   BZ1     5.98      3.90   ! B-D, 0.390  5000
BZ1   BZ2    23.90      2.90   ! D-E, 0.290 20000, Martini 3 benzene TC5-TC5 constraint
BZ2   BZ2    23.90      2.90   ! E-E, 0.290 20000, Martini 3 benzene TC5-TC5 constraint
!bonds for LMA and BMA, 3:1 and 2:1 alkyl beads; force constant of the Martini 2 lipid tail (1250),
!b0 of the Martini 4:1 tail bond (0.47 nm) scaled by the carbons per bead (x 3/4 for 3:3, x 2.5/4 for 3:2)
MAO   LC3     1.49      3.60   ! B-F, 0.360  1250
!bond for HEM; CH2-OH bead centre about 0.30 nm from the ester bead, force constant as QDM
MAO   HOE    17.93      3.00   ! B-H, 0.300 15000
LC3   LC3     1.49      3.60   ! F-F, 0.360  1250
LC3   LC2     1.49      3.00   ! F-G, 0.300  1250
!bonds for PEG/PEO
PEG   PEG    10.0       3.60   ! EO-EO, the distance between two EO units (O-O) as b0


THETAS
!V = V(angle) + V(Urey-Bradley)
!
!V(angle) = Ktheta(Theta - Theta0)**2
!
!V(Urey-Bradley) = Kub(S - S0)**2
!
!Ktheta: kcal/mole/rad**2
!Theta0: degrees
!Kub: kcal/mole/A**2 (Urey-Bradley)
!S0: A
!
!converted from GROMACS type 2, V = 0.5*k*(cos(theta)-cos(theta0))**2 (k in kJ/mol).
!FFs.buildSystem turns these angles into the ReB form
!    V = Ktheta*(theta-theta0)**2/sin(theta)**2
!so the curvature at theta0 is matched by Ktheta = k*sin(theta0)**4/(2*4.184).
!
!atom types     Ktheta    Theta0   Kub     S0
!
!angles for methacrylate polymers (QDM, BZM)
MMA   MMA   MMA    3.23     145.0  ! A-A-A, 145.0 250.0
MMA   MMA   MAO   25.00      90.0   ! A-A-B, 90.0 550.0
MMA   MAO   NC4    4.48     135.0  ! A-B-C, 135.0 150.0
MMA   MAO   BZ1    2.39     135.0  ! A-B-D, 135.0  80.0
MAO   BZ1   BZ2    2.06     130.0  ! B-D-E, 130.0  50.0
!angles for LMA and BMA; side-chain root as BZM; tail from the Martini 2 lipid tail (180.0, 25), with theta0
!moved to 165.0 because the ReB form is singular at 180 (Ktheta = 25*sin(165)**4/8.368)
MMA   MAO   LC3    2.39     135.0  ! A-B-F, 135.0  80.0
!angle for HEM, as QDM
MMA   MAO   HOE    4.48     135.0  ! A-B-H, 135.0 150.0
MAO   LC3   LC3    1.00     165.0  ! B-F-F, 165.0  25.0
LC3   LC3   LC3    1.00     165.0  ! F-F-F, 165.0  25.0
LC3   LC3   LC2    1.00     165.0  ! F-F-G, 165.0  25.0
!angles for PEG/PEO
PEG   PEG   PEG   10.0     123.0  ! EO-EO-EO


PHI
!
!V(dihedral) = Kchi(1 + cos(n(chi) - delta))
!
!Kchi: kcal/mole
!n: multiplicity
!delta: degrees
!
!atom types             Kchi    n   delta
!
!dihedrals for PEG/PEO, zero, kept for PSFs built with auto dihedrals
PEG   PEG   PEG   PEG     0.00    2       0.0    ! EO-EO-EO-EO


IMPHI


NONBONDED  NBXMOD 5  ATOM CDIEL SWITCH VATOM VDISTANCE VSWITCH -
     CUTNB 12.0  CTOFNB 12.0  CTONNB 11.0

!
!V(Lennard-Jones) = Eps,i,j[(Rmin,i,j/ri,j)**12 - 2(Rmin,i,j/ri,j)**6]
!
!epsilon: kcal/mole, Eps,i,j = sqrt(eps,i * eps,j)
!Rmin/2: A, Rmin,i,j = Rmin/2,i + Rmin/2,j
!
!epsilon from the HyRes reference type (MMA and MAO adjusted, see below); Rmin/2 estimated from the number of heavy
!atoms in the bead, following the HyRes side-chain beads
!(1: C3E 2.12, 2: P1S/QdK 2.32-2.36, 3: P1T/A2V 2.62-2.75, 4: QaE/P4Q 2.85-2.89)
!no special 1-4 (as Martini): eps,1-4 and Rmin/2,1-4 equal the normal values
!
!atom  ignored    epsilon      Rmin/2   ignored   eps,1-4       Rmin/2,1-4
!
! for methacrylate polymers (QDM, BZM)
MMA      0.00     -0.1500      2.7000   0.00     -0.1500       2.7000 ! from C3E (-0.1200), adjusted; 3 heavy atoms
MAO      0.00     -0.0600      2.8500   0.00     -0.0600       2.8500 ! from P1T (-0.0502), adjusted; 4 heavy atoms
NC4      0.00     -0.0150      2.9000   0.00     -0.0150       2.9000 ! as QdK, 5 heavy atoms
BZ1      0.00     -0.2208      1.9082   0.00     -0.2208       1.9082 ! A1F eps; Martini 3 tiny bead size (sigma 0.34 nm)
BZ2      0.00     -0.2208      1.9082   0.00     -0.2208       1.9082 ! A1F eps; Martini 3 tiny bead size (sigma 0.34 nm)
! for LMA and BMA
LC3      0.00     -0.2191      2.7541   0.00     -0.2191       2.7541 ! as A2V (Val side chain, C3H7); 3 heavy atoms, also the BMA chain end
LC2      0.00     -0.1700      2.3500   0.00     -0.1700       2.3500 ! between C3E (1 C, -0.120) and A2V (3 C, -0.219); 2 heavy atoms
! for HEM
HOE      0.00     -0.0480      2.3237   0.00     -0.0480       2.3237 ! as P1S (Ser side chain, CH2-OH); 2 heavy atoms
! for PEG/PEO
PEG      0.00     -0.0480      2.6500   0.00     -0.0480       2.6500 ! as P1S, 3 heavy atoms

NBFIX
!                 Emin         Rmin
!                 (kcal/mol)   (A)
! NBFIX for self-interactons to make sure customBNforce is used, instead of the default NBForce, which was deleted
MMA       MMA      -0.1500      5.4000       -0.1500      5.4000
MAO       MAO      -0.0600      5.7000       -0.0600      5.7000
NC4       NC4      -0.0150      5.8000       -0.0150      5.8000
BZ1       BZ1      -0.2208      3.8164       -0.2208      3.8164
BZ2       BZ2      -0.2208      3.8164       -0.2208      3.8164
LC3       LC3      -0.2191      5.5082       -0.2191      5.5082
LC2       LC2      -0.1700      4.7000       -0.1700      4.7000
HOE       HOE      -0.0480      4.6474       -0.0480      4.6474
PEG       PEG      -0.0480      5.3000       -0.0480      5.3000

!# cation-pi of the BZM ring beads, copied from QdK-A3F (4.6877) and QdR-A1F (4.8651); Rmin shifted by the change
!# in Rmin/2 to the Martini 3 tiny bead (1.9082 vs A3F 2.3288 / A1F 2.6414)
!QdK       BZ1      -0.3000      4.8671
!QdR       BZ1      -0.5000      4.8319

END
